WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.500
Let's take a quick look at how to deploy Node.js
applications to Google App Engine. I have

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.910
a Node.js app that runs great on my local
machine. It's important to use the PORT environment

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:17.010
variable as well as "npm start" to run our
code. To deploy our code, go to "cloud.google.com".

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.570
Sign into your Google Account if you haven't
done so already, and then go to "My Console".

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.980
Make sure you sign up for the free trial if
you haven't done that yet. Now go to "select

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.860
a project" and "create a project". Give you
project a name, and click create. Then, go

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.530
to the Compute Engine section, and make sure
Billing is enabled. If you don't have the

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.649
Google Cloud SDK installed on your computer,
see the link in the description for how to

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:44.370
install it. In the same directory as your
"package.json", create a file called "app.yaml"

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.379
with the following information. Run "gcloud
init" to login to your Google Account. Now

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:53.979
run "gcloud preview app deploy" to deploy
your application. In a few minutes, your application

00:00:53.979 --> 00:00:58.429
should be deployed. Go to the URL and you
can see your application running on the cloud!

